2
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,500
Hi, I'm Gigi Murin! I used to be 14 years old in 8th grade, but now I'm not!

3
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,500
I'm a bit clumsy, crazy, and silly,

4
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:48,800
and I may not look it, but actually, I'm a member of Hololive English -Justice-!

5
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,000
That's true.

6
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I call myself the fister, because of my big, big power lift...

7
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:02,000
I don't really like that I call myself the fister, and I don't really know why...

8
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:10,500
...literally called the fister, because I fist people, you know? You know what I mean?

9
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,200
Today is the day of a very important Justice meeting,

10
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,200
but I accidentally overslept!

11
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,000
So I have to hurry up and...

12
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:22,000
...make sure to look both ways before crossing the road, and...

13
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
...go— Aaaah!

14
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:27,500
Gigi goes flying!

15
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Ouch!

16
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:38,200
Who was that? That was so weird.

17
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,000
Wow.

18
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,000
Where am I?

19
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,500
A beautiful 2D fantasy world?

20
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:49,000
That was so efficient. She got hit by a car.

21
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Let me tell you, that was awesome...

22
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:01,200
...hit them with a car, and it would be really cool... Wait, what the—

23
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,500
A horse? That's not a truck!

24
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:06,800
That's dangerous! I could have died!

25
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
But phew! That grem sure knows how to drive.

26
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Grem enja— Aaaah!

27
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Ah... ah...

28
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:26,500
Ouch, my body hurts.

29
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:32,500
I feel like I got run over by something, but I don't know what.

30
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Oh.

31
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:38,200
Is that a statue of a Grem? Looks cool.

32
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Wait a second...

33
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,800
I know this!

34
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,500
I've been isekai'd!

35
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,500
What the freak? Gigi, you're here too?

36
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,800
Is this Justice cardboard?

37
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,200
Gigi, what's going on?

38
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,500
Where are we?

39
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,800
Ouch... What are you guys doing? Why are you cardboard?

40
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Why does CC look so sad?

41
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,500
You f***ing b***h! How dare you do this to me, you b***h!

42
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:11,500
This is your fault somehow! I don't know how you did this, you absolute little dumb f***! Oh, you look terrible.

43
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,200
Rude!

44
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,500
Well, let's go investigate around here.

45
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,500
Let's go.

46
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,500
Okay.

47
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:21,000
I'm on my way! Wait guys! Wait for me!

48
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
We can have an adventure together!

49
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,500
It'll be so fun, and, and, and...

50
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Wait, wait, wait... What's going on?

51
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Aaaah!

52
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:37,500
Horses...

53
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:41,500
Two of them...

54
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Aaaah!

55
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,500
Goodbye...

56
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:00,000
Leaving heartbreak of the past behind.

57
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,808
Turning back, it's time.

58
00:05:01,808 --> 00:05:05,108
Moving down our own paths,

59
00:05:05,108 --> 00:05:11,808
ever voyaging forward to make this journey last.

60
00:05:29,808 --> 00:05:33,208
Never spoken about in the light,

61
00:05:33,208 --> 00:05:37,008
like a promise found riding the wind.

62
00:05:37,008 --> 00:05:40,808
Where a myth begins spiraling outward and up,

63
00:05:40,808 --> 00:05:44,508
an inspiring tale begins.

64
00:05:44,508 --> 00:05:48,308
Who would dare defy changing of times,

65
00:05:48,308 --> 00:05:51,808
as we follow unreachable dreams?

66
00:05:51,808 --> 00:05:55,508
No, it's here and right now that we're drawn to somehow,

67
00:05:55,508 --> 00:06:00,008
deep inside, a will to live that won't leave.

68
00:06:00,008 --> 00:06:03,208
Let our fates awaken...

69
00:06:03,208 --> 00:06:07,008
Wandering near and far,

70
00:06:07,008 --> 00:06:10,508
touching lives just like ours.

71
00:06:10,508 --> 00:06:15,508
Guiding fire till life's wasted away.

72
00:06:15,508 --> 00:06:18,008
One day,

73
00:06:18,008 --> 00:06:21,008
I'll recall these nights,

74
00:06:21,008 --> 00:06:24,508
our relentless honesty.

75
00:06:24,508 --> 00:06:28,008
Pressing onward,

76
00:06:28,008 --> 00:06:31,508
we never surrender.

77
00:06:31,508 --> 00:06:35,008
Toward the skies,

78
00:06:35,008 --> 00:06:40,008
we can rise again.

79
00:06:40,008 --> 00:06:49,008
Again...

80
00:06:52,008 --> 00:07:00,008
I was hit by a truck and reincarnated as the protagonist in a fantasy world but then a horse ran me over and now all my friends are cardboard?
[Title: I was hit by a truck and reincarnated as the protagonist in a fantasy world but then a horse ran me over and now all my friends are cardboard?]

81
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:08,008
Uuugh...

82
00:07:08,008 --> 00:07:12,008
If anything else hits me, I don't think I'll survive much longer.

83
00:07:12,008 --> 00:07:14,208
I really need to be more careful.

84
00:07:14,208 --> 00:07:17,508
Thank goodness I'm still alive.

85
00:07:19,508 --> 00:07:24,008
The winds whispered of your coming...

86
00:07:24,008 --> 00:07:28,008
And now, here you are.

87
00:07:28,508 --> 00:07:30,508
Who are you?!

88
00:07:31,008 --> 00:07:36,508
I am the greatest wizard in all of Grem Kingdom!

89
00:07:36,508 --> 00:07:39,008
Wizard Oji-chan.

90
00:07:39,008 --> 00:07:44,208
Wizard Oji-chan? Are you a wizard or Oji-chan? Do you have a name? What should I call you?

91
00:07:46,008 --> 00:07:54,008
So many of Grem's warriors have fallen, one by one, while we waited for your arrival...

92
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:56,508
The wait was worth it!

93
00:07:56,508 --> 00:08:03,008
You are far more powerful than I ever imagined a hero could be!

94
00:08:03,508 --> 00:08:08,008
He's not responding to me. He's probably an NPC. Is this like a game? Am I in a game?

95
00:08:08,508 --> 00:08:10,508
NPC?!

96
00:08:10,508 --> 00:08:16,008
NPC? Show some respect! I'm a noble wizard! Oji-chan!

97
00:08:16,008 --> 00:08:20,508
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

98
00:08:21,008 --> 00:08:24,508
I'm sorry, I didn't know you could talk!

99
00:08:25,008 --> 00:08:27,508
You're the key.

100
00:08:27,508 --> 00:08:34,508
Without you, your friend and this world are lost...

101
00:08:34,508 --> 00:08:38,008
What? Lost? What are you talking about?

102
00:08:38,008 --> 00:08:42,508
Gigi, the world is waiting...

103
00:08:42,508 --> 00:08:50,008
He knows my name! That's me. I'm the hero. I'm gonna save the world from being cardboard.

104
00:08:52,008 --> 00:08:55,008
Hazaah!

105
00:08:56,508 --> 00:09:00,508
What did you do to me?! It hurts! It hurts!

106
00:09:00,808 --> 00:09:05,508
あれ？おかしい。何言ってんだ。これ。おかしい。
Wait... strange. What are you saying? Why...

107
00:09:05,508 --> 00:09:08,508
Hazaah!

108
00:09:09,508 --> 00:09:16,508
Wow, I feel so cute and soft and fluffy now! Friends with you? Purchase next time they're in stock.

109
00:09:16,508 --> 00:09:20,008
あ、気持ち悪い？ごめん。もう一回やらせて。ちゃんと、今度、今度ちゃんとやるから。
Ah, do you feel sick? Sorry. Let me try once more. I'll do it properly this time!

110
00:09:20,008 --> 00:09:21,508
I don't understand...

111
00:09:21,508 --> 00:09:22,008
オッケー、オッケー。
Okay, okay.

112
00:09:22,008 --> 00:09:28,008
Haaaaazaah!

113
00:09:28,008 --> 00:09:31,008
Hazaah!

114
00:09:31,508 --> 00:09:36,508
Squeak! Squeak squeak! Squeak!

115
00:09:36,508 --> 00:09:41,008
一回、一回！オッケー、オッケー、アイムレディー！
Once more, once more! Okay, okay, I'm ready!

116
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:45,008
ジシ！ジシ？レディー！バー！
Jishi! Jishi? Ready! Baaa!

117
00:09:45,008 --> 00:09:48,008
Hazaah!

118
00:09:49,008 --> 00:09:55,008
Ah... ah... ah...

119
00:09:55,008 --> 00:09:59,008
Oh wait, I think I can move now! What is...

120
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:01,316
What is this?

121
00:10:02,516 --> 00:10:04,116
Hands?!

122
00:10:04,116 --> 00:10:07,416
You did it! You've done it!

123
00:10:07,416 --> 00:10:08,516
Oh my god!

124
00:10:08,516 --> 00:10:11,816
Look how... how cute I am!

125
00:10:11,816 --> 00:10:15,816
Aw, I've always been cute. But now, now it's even- now everyone can see how cute I-

126
00:10:15,816 --> 00:10:18,816
Look at that fat tail! Look at that fat ta-

127
00:10:18,816 --> 00:10:20,116
I can do everything!

128
00:10:20,116 --> 00:10:21,816
I can't do that.

129
00:10:21,816 --> 00:10:24,416
Watch this, guys. Have you ever seen this before?

130
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:25,516
Okay, okay.

131
00:10:25,516 --> 00:10:28,516
Whee! Whee! I can do everything.

132
00:10:28,516 --> 00:10:30,416
Two in a row? Just kidding.

133
00:10:30,416 --> 00:10:32,416
I have a world to save.

134
00:10:32,416 --> 00:10:34,316
Look at that, everyone loves me!

135
00:10:34,316 --> 00:10:38,516
Gigi Murin!

136
00:10:39,216 --> 00:10:43,016
おっ、疲れた。よいしょ。
Oh, I'm tired. There we go.

137
00:10:48,016 --> 00:10:51,116
Oh, I'm so dizzy.

138
00:10:53,016 --> 00:10:54,816
Oh, I'm sorry.

139
00:10:54,816 --> 00:10:57,616
What... what should I do to save everyone?

140
00:10:59,816 --> 00:11:05,116
Oh, the world is spinning. Owy.

141
00:11:05,516 --> 00:11:08,016
Before saving everyone...

142
00:11:08,016 --> 00:11:11,816
...let's see if you can survive basic chores.

143
00:11:11,816 --> 00:11:13,916
Basic... I can do basic chores.

144
00:11:15,816 --> 00:11:18,716
Let's start with...

145
00:11:18,716 --> 00:11:21,016
Huh?

146
00:11:21,016 --> 00:11:23,016
Start with what? Start with what?

147
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:24,016
What?

148
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:25,316
What are we starting with?

149
00:11:25,316 --> 00:11:26,516
What?

150
00:11:26,516 --> 00:11:27,716
What?

151
00:11:27,716 --> 00:11:29,016
Wing?

152
00:11:29,016 --> 00:11:31,016
Birds! Birds! What?

153
00:11:31,016 --> 00:11:32,816
Wait, what?

154
00:11:32,816 --> 00:11:34,816
Old geezer! What are you doing with the birds? Wait!

155
00:11:34,816 --> 00:11:36,516
Wait! Wait! Wait!

156
00:11:36,516 --> 00:11:39,016
Old geezer, don't! Don't!

157
00:11:39,016 --> 00:11:41,516
Wait, wait, wait!

158
00:11:41,516 --> 00:11:43,316
Wait!

159
00:11:43,316 --> 00:11:45,316
No!

160
00:11:45,316 --> 00:11:49,016
Aaaaah!

161
00:11:49,016 --> 00:11:54,816
The birds took him! I knew I could never trust a bird!

162
00:11:54,816 --> 00:11:58,016
Hey you, Come here! Follow me!

163
00:11:58,016 --> 00:12:00,016
Um...

164
00:12:00,016 --> 00:12:02,816
I have to help my... my friend.

165
00:12:02,816 --> 00:12:06,616
You're scared and lost... Not knowing what to do, right?

166
00:12:06,616 --> 00:12:10,116
I'll show you how to save your friends. Follow me!

167
00:12:10,116 --> 00:12:11,716
Oh, okay.

168
00:12:11,716 --> 00:12:14,316
You're so small.

169
00:12:24,316 --> 00:12:26,516
This is weird.

170
00:12:28,016 --> 00:12:31,116
This place is dark and it smells bad.

171
00:12:31,116 --> 00:12:35,316
Hey it smells good!!!! Do exactly as I say if you want to save your friends!

172
00:12:35,316 --> 00:12:39,516
Go to the Grem Kingdom and return with the One Ping, a Honkshoe, and a Straw Hat.

173
00:12:39,516 --> 00:12:41,516
Why do you need them?

174
00:12:41,516 --> 00:12:44,716
YOU DON'T GET TO ASK ME ANY QUESTIONS!!! NOW GO GIGI, GOOOOOO!!

175
00:12:47,316 --> 00:12:49,016
Okay.

176
00:13:01,316 --> 00:13:03,016
Wow!

177
00:13:03,016 --> 00:13:06,016
So this is the Grem Kingdom?

178
00:13:06,016 --> 00:13:09,516
It's so cool! There's so many Grems!

179
00:13:09,516 --> 00:13:13,516
Does this mean this entire kingdom is mine if I save it?

180
00:13:14,716 --> 00:13:16,816
Wow, so many of you.

181
00:13:17,316 --> 00:13:20,516
Oh, not all at once! No, no, no, no.

182
00:13:20,516 --> 00:13:21,816
What?

183
00:13:21,816 --> 00:13:24,016
Oh, I can't hear you.

184
00:13:24,016 --> 00:13:28,016
Let's... let's try this Grem. Lucky little Grem, what's on your mind?

185
00:13:28,016 --> 00:13:33,016
Things aren't going well with my partner... I need your help to fix our relationship.

186
00:13:33,016 --> 00:13:36,516
Aw... That is not my problem.

187
00:13:36,516 --> 00:13:39,516
Ah, okay. How about this Grem? Do you have anything interesting to say to me?

188
00:13:41,516 --> 00:13:47,516
My tummy is getting very large and I don't know why. Please come with me to the doctor.

189
00:13:48,816 --> 00:13:52,516
Okay, a little... little secret. Pregnant.

190
00:13:52,516 --> 00:13:54,516
Okay, how about this one?

191
00:13:55,316 --> 00:13:59,516
Make a contract with me, and become a magical girl!

192
00:13:59,516 --> 00:14:03,016
Oh, that is not my problem either. Oh, no, no, no, no.

193
00:14:03,016 --> 00:14:07,016
I will not be doing that. I know what happens when you sign a contract!

194
00:14:07,016 --> 00:14:10,016
You should never put your name down on things.

195
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:12,516
Well, these Grems were useless.

196
00:14:13,316 --> 00:14:16,016
I think if I use my RPG knowledge...

197
00:14:16,016 --> 00:14:19,516
...you're supposed to get information from NPCs...

198
00:14:19,516 --> 00:14:24,016
...at a store! And there are so many stalls near me.

199
00:14:24,016 --> 00:14:26,016
Ah! Let's go to this one.

200
00:14:28,516 --> 00:14:31,016
[Gasp] So cute! Aw...

201
00:14:31,016 --> 00:14:35,016
Are you a little worker Grem? Are you?

202
00:14:35,016 --> 00:14:37,516
How much do you make an hour?

203
00:14:37,516 --> 00:14:40,516
Do you make enough to survive? Aw...

204
00:14:40,516 --> 00:14:43,016
Oh, what is this?

205
00:14:43,016 --> 00:14:45,016
For me?

206
00:14:46,816 --> 00:14:50,016
Uh, that's decorative hay, not edible...

207
00:14:54,016 --> 00:14:56,016
Can I ask you something?

208
00:14:56,816 --> 00:14:59,016
Oh, what is this? Dialogue.

209
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,324
Box?

210
00:15:01,324 --> 00:15:03,024
Um...

211
00:15:03,024 --> 00:15:06,024
Where can I get The One Ping?

212
00:15:07,024 --> 00:15:08,824
Oh, you are looking for the One Ping?

213
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:13,524
Then, here is the Quest for you! Take this ring and throw it into a volcano to destroy it.

214
00:15:13,524 --> 00:15:20,524
This cursed ring holds centuries of anger. To purify it, it must be thrown into a volcano... but we fear fire and can't go near it.

215
00:15:20,524 --> 00:15:22,024
Hmm.

216
00:15:22,024 --> 00:15:24,024
Oh, okay. Yeah!

217
00:15:24,024 --> 00:15:26,524
I- I can do that quest for you.

218
00:15:26,524 --> 00:15:29,824
Don't worry, I am the Chosen One!

219
00:15:29,824 --> 00:15:30,824
Ah!

220
00:15:30,824 --> 00:15:32,424
A ring!

221
00:15:32,424 --> 00:15:34,224
Wow!

222
00:15:34,224 --> 00:15:35,824
I don't know what a volcano is.

223
00:15:35,824 --> 00:15:38,824
How is this supposed to help me save Justice?

224
00:15:38,824 --> 00:15:41,024
They're gonna die!

225
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:43,024
They're gonna die if the volcano erupts!

226
00:15:43,024 --> 00:15:44,224
Oh, wait. I don't know what a volcano is.

227
00:15:44,224 --> 00:15:46,824
Let's just try to find the One Ping myself.

228
00:15:48,524 --> 00:15:51,324
This box is a little suspicious.

229
00:15:52,524 --> 00:15:54,024
Hmm...

230
00:15:54,024 --> 00:15:58,524
Deliver to Weapon Shop.

231
00:15:59,024 --> 00:16:01,424
Oh, cool! Is this for a quest?

232
00:16:03,524 --> 00:16:05,424
